From 74470910fd4f063c446a4fe6e1136aa5d7d0ec2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] display: HDR output

aurora_set_hdr(enabled, paperWhiteNits, highlightBoost): when the window is
on a display with HDR on (SDL_PROP_WINDOW_HDR_ENABLED_BOOLEAN) and the
backend can show it (D3D12/D3D11: a float16 swapchain is scRGB; Metal: the
CAMetalLayer made EDR in extended linear sRGB), the surface is configured
RGBA16Float. Everything else keeps the internal SDR format: the present
blit and ImGui draw into a surface-sized SDR target, and a last pass
linearises it, scales its white to the paper white (scRGB 1.0 = 80 nits;
EDR 1.0 taken as 100 nits), raises what is near white by up to the boost
and clamps to the display's headroom. Off, or unsupported: SDR as before.
aurora_hdr_supported / aurora_hdr_active for the application, all in
include/aurora/hdr.h (not display.h, so 0013 keeps reverse-applying);
SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED reconfigures the surface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LCrnrpyxCzFfKcsiso9KdP
